.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH run 1  "run " 
.SH NAME
run \- Run a snippet by name
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrun\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-step\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> [\fIKEY=value\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a snippet by name
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and execute nothing (alias: \-\-dry)
.TP
\fB\-\-step\fR
Confirm each step before running it (steps mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
Do not write fetched snippets to the run cache
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Run from the local cache only; never fetch
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Snippet name, or `owner/name` / `name@version` for a cloud snippet (Step 13)
.TP
[\fIKEY=value\fR]
KEY=value variable assignments
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg run ubuntu\-setup
  fg ubuntu\-setup            (shorthand)
  fg alice/deploy \-\-dry\-run
